{
  "language": "en",
  "_readme": [
    "Vocabulary lives in 'pools' and 'bossPools'. Nothing else in the game",
    "hardcodes a word. To add vocabulary, drop it in the pool it belongs to --",
    "no code change is needed.",
    "",
    "Pools are length bands: tiny 2-3, short 4-5, medium 6-7, long 8-10,",
    "epic 11+. 'tricky' is the exception -- it is graded by how awkward a word",
    "is to TYPE rather than how long it is (repeated letters, uncommon",
    "digraphs, long finger travel), so it deliberately overlaps the others.",
    "",
    "Boss ranks: novice 5-7, adept 8-10, master 11-13, legend 14+. Boss words",
    "are reserved -- they never appear in the ordinary pools, so a climactic",
    "word cannot already have turned up on a Beisach in level two.",
    "",
    "'difficulties' is the tuning table, not more word lists: for each tier, a",
    "list of level bands saying which pools that stretch of the run may draw",
    "from and which boss rank its bosses use. Bands match by 'throughLevel' in",
    "order, and the last band also covers everything past it. Making an early",
    "level gentler is an edit here, never in Java.",
    "",
    "'bossParagraphs' holds the finale. Each tier has several three-sentence",
    "paragraphs; one is drawn per run. Sentence one, two, three are the three",
    "",
    "'projectile' is 2-3 letters and must stay that way -- it is shared by thrown bolts and power-up pickups, and a bolt gives you barely a second. Four letters there is a real difficulty change, not a tweak.",
    "stages of the fight."
  ],
